NAME
    ip - show the network interface and its addressing

SYNOPSIS
    ip [OBJECT]

DESCRIPTION
    Shows the addressing of the machine's network interface, eth0.
    With no OBJECT, or with addr, it prints the link state, the MAC
    address and the IPv4 address with its netmask and broadcast
    address. link prints only the link and MAC; route prints the
    default gateway and the on-link route.

    OBJECT may be abbreviated the way iproute2 abbreviates it: a for
    addr, l for link, r for route.

    The address, netmask and gateway are those of QEMU's slirp user
    network (10.0.2.15/24, gateway 10.0.2.2) and are fixed by the
    kernel; ip reports them, it does not change them. The interface
    counters are in /proc/net/dev.

OBJECT
    addr (a)     interface address (default)
    link (l)     link layer: state and MAC address
    route (r)    routing table

FILES
    /proc/net/dev   interface byte and packet counters

EXIT STATUS
    0 on success, 1 on a bad object or when there is no network
    interface.

SEE ALSO
    ping(1), fetch(1)
